{"id":"v1_ChdQQnJJYXZxYUNPLUR6N0lQbzdIYzJRdxIXUEJySWF2cWFDTy1EejdJUG83SGMyUXc","status":"completed","usage":{"total_tokens":4019,"total_input_tokens":132,"input_tokens_by_modality":[{"modality":"text","tokens":132}],"total_cached_tokens":0,"total_output_tokens":161,"total_tool_use_tokens":3423,"tool_use_tokens_by_modality":[{"modality":"text","tokens":3423}],"total_thought_tokens":303,"raw_prompt_token":3554,"model_invocation_token_counts":[{"prompt_tokens_details":[{"modality":"text","tokens":452}],"candidates_tokens_details":[{"modality":"text","tokens":30}],"thoughts_tokens_details":[{"modality":"text","tokens":97}]},{"prompt_tokens_details":[{"modality":"text","tokens":3554}],"candidates_tokens_details":[{"modality":"text","tokens":141}],"thoughts_tokens_details":[{"modality":"text","tokens":206}]}],"non_grounding_model_invocation_token_counts":[{"prompt_tokens_details":[{"modality":"text","tokens":452}],"candidates_tokens_details":[{"modality":"text","tokens":30}],"thoughts_tokens_details":[{"modality":"text","tokens":97}]},{"prompt_tokens_details":[{"modality":"text","tokens":3554}],"candidates_tokens_details":[{"modality":"text","tokens":141}],"thoughts_tokens_details":[{"modality":"text","tokens":206}]}]},"created":"2026-10-08T22:33:42Z","updated":"2026-10-08T22:33:42Z","service_tier":"standard","steps":[{"id":"call_1361037","signature":"","type":"file_search_call"},{"call_id":"call_1361037","signature":"","type":"file_search_result"},{"signature":"","type":"thought"},{"content":[{"text":"According to Augustus Le Plongeon’s narrative in *Vestiges of the Mayas*, the territory known as **Tierra de Guerra** is situated between:\n\n* **Guatemala**\n* **Tabasco**\n* **Chiapas**\n* **Yucatan**\n\nIn this geographical context, it is described as a zealously guarded stronghold in well-nigh inaccessible valleys defended by towering mountain ranges, with part of the territory being watered by the **Uzumasinta** (Usumacinta) River.","annotations":[{"start_index":0,"end_index":139,"document_uri":"fileSearchStores/graphragbench-9lax22b99qlk","file_name":"Novel-30752.txt","source":"the ancient customs of the aborigines, were unable to destroy it; nay, they were obliged to learn it; and now many of their descendants have forgotten the mother tongue of their sires, and speak Maya only. In some localities in Central America it is still spoken in its pristine purity, as, for example, by the _Chaacmules_, a tribe of bearded men, it is said, who live in the vicinity of the unexplored ruins of the ancient city of _Tekal_. It is a well-known fact that many tribes, as that of the Itzaes, retreating before the Nahualt invaders, after the surrender and destruction of their cities, sought refuge in the islands of the lake _Peten_ of to-day, and called it _Petenitza_, the _islands of the Itzaes_; or in the well nigh inaccessible valleys, defended by ranges of towering mountains. There they live to-day, preserving the customs, manners, language of their forefathers unaltered, in the tract of land known to us as _Tierra de Guerra_. No white man has ever penetrated their zealously guarded stronghold that lays between Guatemala, Tabasco, Chiapas and Yucatan, the river _Uzumasinta_ watering part of their territory. The Maya language seems to be one of the oldest tongues","custom_metadata":{"source":"Novel-30752"},"type":"file_citation"},{"start_index":142,"end_index":157,"document_uri":"fileSearchStores/graphragbench-9lax22b99qlk","file_name":"Novel-30752.txt","source":"the ancient customs of the aborigines, were unable to destroy it; nay, they were obliged to learn it; and now many of their descendants have forgotten the mother tongue of their sires, and speak Maya only. In some localities in Central America it is still spoken in its pristine purity, as, for example, by the _Chaacmules_, a tribe of bearded men, it is said, who live in the vicinity of the unexplored ruins of the ancient city of _Tekal_. It is a well-known fact that many tribes, as th